<article class="env-lemma" id="0H3L">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0H3L">Lemma <span data-tag="0H3L">29.56.3</span>.</a> Let $A \to B$ be a ring map inducing a dominant morphism $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(B) \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ of spectra. There exists an $A$-subalgebra $B' \subset B$ such that </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(B') \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ is a universal homeomorphism inducing isomorphisms on residue fields, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
given a factorization $A \to C \to B$ such that $\mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(C) \to \mathop{\mathrm{Spec}}(A)$ is a universal homeomorphism inducing isomorphisms on residue fields, the image of $C \to B$ is contained in $B'$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This proof is exactly the same as the proof of Lemma <a href="/tag/0H3J" data-tag="0H3J">29.56.1</a> except we use Proposition <a href="/tag/0CND" data-tag="0CND">29.47.7</a> in stead of Proposition <a href="/tag/0CNE" data-tag="0CNE">29.47.8</a> 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>